---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Copyright & Report Content | Linespedia" 
  description="Report copyright concerns, content issues, or request removal on Linespedia. We take intellectual property rights seriously."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-24 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-serif font-black mb-12 text-primary">Copyright & Report Content</h1>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-indigo max-w-none text-primary/80">
      <p>
        Linespedia is committed to respecting intellectual property rights and maintaining a trustworthy platform. 
        This page outlines how to report content concerns, copyright issues, and request removals.
      </p>

      <h2>Copyright Infringement Report (DMCA)</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe that content on Linespedia infringes on a copyright you own or control, 
        please submit a report with the following information:
      </p>

      <div class="bg-amber-50/40 backdrop-blur-md rounded-2xl p-8 border border-amber-100/30 not-prose space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-primary font-bold text-lg">Required Information for Copyright Reports:</h3>
        <ol class="text-primary/80 space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside">
          <li><strong>Your Information:</strong> Full name, email address, and contact information</li>
          <li><strong>Content Location:</strong> URL of the allegedly infringing content</li>
          <li><strong>Copyright Ownership:</strong> Description of your copyright and proof of ownership</li>
          <li><strong>Infringing Content:</strong> Description of how the content infringes your copyright</li>
          <li><strong>Good Faith Statement:</strong> Statement that you have a good faith belief the use is unauthorized</li>
          <li><strong>Legal Statement:</strong> Statement that the information provided is accurate and you are authorized to act</li>
          <li><strong>Your Signature:</strong> Physical or electronic signature</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <h2>How to Submit a Report</h2>
      <p>
        Please send copyright reports and content concerns to us via our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the subject line, clearly indicate: <code>Copyright Report</code> or <code>Content Removal Request</code>
      </p>

      <h2>Content Moderation Report</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe content violates our policies, is inappropriate, or should be removed for reasons 
        other than copyright, please include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>URL of the content in question</li>
        <li>Reason for the report (describe the concern)</li>
        <li>Your contact information</li>
        <li>Any supporting evidence or context</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Attribution & Rights Concerns</h2>
      <p>
        If you notice:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Incorrect attribution of authorship</li>
        <li>Missing proper source citation</li>
        <li>Inaccurate copyright or license information</li>
        <li>Violations of author rights or permissions</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please report these issues using our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> with details and evidence.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Response Process</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Receipt:</strong> We acknowledge receipt of your report within 2 business days</li>
        <li><strong>Investigation:</strong> We investigate the claim thoroughly (typically 5-10 business days)</li>
        <li><strong>Determination:</strong> We determine the appropriate action based on our policies and legal obligations</li>
        <li><strong>Action:</strong> We take appropriate action, which may include:
          <ul>
            <li>Removing or modifying content</li>
            <li>Adding or correcting attribution</li>
            <li>Requesting additional information from the reporter</li>
            <li>Declining the report if we determine it lacks merit</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Notification:</strong> We notify you of the outcome via email</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Content Attribution on Linespedia</h2>
      <p>
        Every poem on Linespedia includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Author name and attribution</li>
        <li>Public domain status (where applicable)</li>
        <li>Copyright or license information</li>
        <li>Source attribution when not original work</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If you notice missing or incorrect information, please <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Rights We Respect</h2>
      <p>
        Linespedia respects:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Copyright and intellectual property rights</li>
        <li>Author moral rights and attribution</li>
        <li>License terms and conditions</li>
        <li>Privacy and personal rights</li>
        <li>Community standards and policies</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Public Domain Content</h2>
      <p>
        Many poems on Linespedia are in the public domain (works by classic poets where copyright has expired). 
        For public domain works, we still provide:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Accurate author attribution</li>
        <li>Publication date and source information</li>
        <li>Clear indication of public domain status</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Dispute Resolution</h2>
      <p>
        If you disagree with our determination on a report, you may request a review by 
        <a href="/contact/">contacting us</a> with:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your original report or reference number</li>
        <li>Explanation of why you disagree with our decision</li>
        <li>Any additional evidence or information</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>False Reports</h2>
      <p>
        We take false or malicious reports seriously. Submitting knowingly false reports may result in:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Termination of your ability to submit reports</li>
        <li>Legal action as permitted by law</li>
        <li>Other consequences as appropriate</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
      <p>
        We are committed to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Treating all reports fairly and seriously</li>
        <li>Responding promptly to legitimate concerns</li>
        <li>Protecting the rights of content creators</li>
        <li>Maintaining accuracy and proper attribution</li>
        <li>Operating transparently in our processes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related Pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/about/">About Linespedia</a> - Learn about our mission and values</li>
        <li><a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a> - General inquiries and feedback</li>
        <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> - How we handle your data</li>
        <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> - Our terms and conditions</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="my-12" />

      <p class="text-sm text-primary/60">
        Last updated: May 9, 2026<br/>
        If you have questions about this policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
